This data set contains, and is derived from, the following sources. Anyone
redistributing it, whole or in part, credits them as below.


1. Bundeslebensmittelschlüssel (BLS) 4.0
   Max Rubner-Institut (MRI), Bundesforschungsinstitut für Ernährung und
   Lebensmittel, release 2025. https://blsdb.de
   Licence: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Changes: reduced to 16 nutrient fields per 100 g (Data/sources/bls.json
   keeps every row with those fields), and linked to kitchen words, spellings,
   varieties, measures and aisles; the app ships the rows the catalog names.
   Where VITAA is blank, VITA stands in. The nutrient values themselves are
   unchanged. The catalog refers to them by SBLS code.
   Where a row leaves a nutrient blank and the food by nature carries next to
   none of it, the app counts the blank as 0 (Data/assumed-zeros.yaml); no
   value the BLS states is changed.


2. Table de composition nutritionnelle des aliments Ciqual 2020 and 2025
   Anses (Agence nationale de sécurité sanitaire de l'alimentation, de
   l'environnement et du travail), France. https://ciqual.anses.fr
   Licence: Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0 (Etalab), which is compatible
   with CC BY 4.0.

   Used for single rows the BLS does not have, copied by hand with their
   Ciqual number and name as published; Data/sources/ciqual-2020.json and
   ciqual-2025.json keep every row of the tables with the 16 fields.


3. USDA FoodData Central, SR Legacy (April 2018) and Foundation Foods
   (December 2025)
   U.S. Department of Agriculture, Agricultural Research Service.
   https://fdc.nal.usda.gov
   Licence: CC0 1.0 (public domain), https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

   Used for single rows the BLS does not have, with their FDC ID and name as
   published; Data/sources/usda-*.json keep every row with the 16 fields.


4. Nutrition declarations of retail products
   Where no database lists a food, a row may be read from a product's
   nutrition declaration. A declaration is a statement of fact and carries no
   licence. Each such row is a row of Data/sources/labels.json, keyed by the
   product's EAN, so it can be checked at the shelf.


Every source is registered in Data/sources/<id>.yaml, with its rows in
Data/sources/<id>.json. An ingredient names a row by the source's id and its
code there, and the app shows both under the ingredient as „Quelle: …“. The
settings' "Datenquellen" page shows every source of the register.
